{
  "help" : {
    "overview" : "^#f3d36a;<Needs help>^reset; Type ^cyan;/oneeds help <topic>^reset;. Topics: needs, tiers, drinks, foods, hygiene, sleep, settings, commands.",
    "needs" : "Needs tracks four values from 0 to 100. Thirst, Fatigue, and Bladder get worse as they rise. Hygiene is reversed: 100 is clean and 0 is filthy, and the HUD shows Dirtiness as 100 minus Hygiene.",
    "tiers" : "Thresholds: Noticeable 50, Serious 70, Urgent 85, Critical 95. Crossing upward warns once. Consequences scale speed, jump, power, energy regeneration, and protection with safety floors, and never deal direct damage.",
    "drinks" : "Drinks restore Thirst and add Bladder. Coffee delays Fatigue with caffeine, alcohol leaves you tired, and salty or toxic drinks worsen Thirst. Bottled Water returns an Empty Bottle. Use /oneeds beverage <itemName> and /oneeds beverages [all|details].",
    "foods" : "Eating affects Thirst, Bladder, and Fatigue through food profiles (meal, heavy, snack, sugary, juicy, salty, rawmeat, toxic, caffeinated). Use /oneeds food <itemName> and /oneeds foods [all|details].",
    "hygiene" : "Dirtiness rises with running, jumping, combat, dirty liquids, and harsh biomes. Clean water, rain, showers, and baths restore Hygiene. Lounging on a toilet relieves Bladder. Environmental multipliers default to 1 for unknown biomes.",
    "sleep" : "Sleep in a bed to restore Fatigue in about three minutes at Normal speed; change Sleep recovery in /oneeds options. A long enough sleep grants a Rested bonus that slows awake Fatigue gain. Day/night and hot or cold biomes also affect Thirst and Fatigue. Needs never change the game speed.",
    "settings" : "Run /oneeds options to open the in-game settings panel. It controls HUD options, gameplay toggles (warnings, consequences, feedback, day/night fatigue, rested bonus, environment effects), and the difficulty and sleep recovery selectors.",
    "commands" : "^#f3d36a;<Needs commands>^reset; Local testing and diagnostics:"
  },
